      "section": "Operational Glossary And Copy Audit > Language Policy",
      "lineStart": 28,
      "lineEnd": 38,
      "text": "## Language Policy - Operator surfaces may expose code / enum values in diagnostics, but visible UI labels must use one shared meaning per workflow concept. - Traditional Chinese copy must stay in Traditional Chinese. Avoid mixing in Simplified Chinese variants such as `運營`. - Code literals such as `recording_pending` remain acceptable in audit, developer, and runbook contexts when the exact contract value matters. - User-facing labels should translate the concept, then optionally preserve the literal code in a note or evidence view when required.",
